From 4971499562e4e47d9c7c941074f0e54aa17faa51 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 22:54:16 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] Add group auto-join, invite-code regeneration, and
 email-restricted invite links

- groups.autoJoinEnabled toggle: when on, students who join by group code
  are added ACTIVE immediately instead of going through teacher approval
- teacher can regenerate a group's join code (revokes the old one)
- new group_email_invites table: a one-time, email-restricted invite link
  (hashed token, 7-day expiry, revoke/resend) that a teacher shares
  manually (there is no outbound email sending in this codebase) via the
  existing ShareBox copy/WhatsApp/Telegram/QR flow
- public preview + student accept flow at /invite/:token, mirroring the
  existing /join/:inviteCode flow
- only the SHA-256 hash of the invite token is ever persisted; the raw
  token is returned once, at creation/resend time
- inviteDisplayStatus() derives EXPIRED from a still-PENDING row without
  a DB write, matching the existing pure derived-state convention
  (server/modules/activity.ts, engine.ts) - unit tested

Schema change only: migration 0005_group_invites_v2.sql is NOT applied
here. Per the product spec this implements, migrations must be run
manually against DATABASE_URL (pnpm db:migrate) - nothing here deploys
automatically or touches production data.

